/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475943 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (1,2)}\\,\\frac{(x-1)(y-2)}{(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nI. The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=2$\n\nII. The limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{2}$ along the path $y=x+1$\n\nIII. The limit does not exist" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475943 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "83c8f2ad-db17-53f8-868d-e48deabc8feb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475943 #edb/ref 1074 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,2)}\\,\\frac{(x-1)(y-2)}{(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}} & =\\frac{(1-1)(2-2)}{(1-1)^{2}+(2-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0(0)}{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(1,2)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement I is true. Taking $x\\to (1,2)$ along the path $y=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,2)\\,\\,\\,y=2}\\,\\frac{(x-1)(y-2)}{(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\,\\frac{(x-1)(2-2)}{(x-1)^{2}+(2-2)^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\,\\frac{(x-1)(0)}{(x-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Taking $x\\to (1,2)$ along the path $y=x+1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,2)\\,\\,\\,y=x+1}\\,\\frac{(x-1)(y-2)}{(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{(x-1)(x+1-2)}{(x-1)^{2}+(x+1-2)^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{(x-1)(x-1)}{(x-1)^{2}+(x-1)^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2(x-1)^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\cancel{(x-1)^{2}}}{2\\cancel{(x-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (1,2)}\\,\\frac{(x-1)(y-2)}{(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}}=\\text{DNE}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475988 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186475990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475988 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "13485a67-00ba-5d4e-a4ce-60195066ea29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475988 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186377695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475990 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186475997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475990 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3925855e-b8a5-539c-a189-1799c0ceb8ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475990 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186345001 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475994 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186475998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475994 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5c7e6dac-de5a-50c9-a4a3-207c8cf4283a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475994 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186380242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475997 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186475994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475997 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a1d76783-98ca-587b-9e64-3ae5ae7e97c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475997 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186345003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475998 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d56691a3-bd81-5d30-bd36-57d7d11c4bf9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475998 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186475943 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
